+### Turning it off (local patch)
+
+`/secret-box off` stops hiding keys in prompts and tool output, and stops refusing `.env` commits and `@.env`. `/secret-box on` turns both back on, `/secret-box` alone flips it, and `/secret-box status` says which it is. Only you can turn it off: a scheduled prompt, a message from another session or another mod can't. A restart returns to the `enabled` setting. While it is off, the box still works, placeholders already in the conversation still become real values, and a value handed to a tool that way is still hidden if the tool prints it. Anything else a tool prints while it is off stays in the transcript as it was printed.
+
